Check vaSyncSurface() before importing the surface.

qffmpeghwaccel_vaapi.cpp exports the surface handle (checked), then calls
vaSyncSurface() IGNORING its status — the code's own "### Check" comment sits
right above it. Importing an unsynchronized/failed surface hands the render
pipeline undefined pixel data (the corrupt-packet storms that trigger the
0001 defect produce exactly these sync failures). On failure, bail to the
non-zero-copy path; the existing QScopeGuard already closes the exported fds.

--- a/src/plugins/multimedia/ffmpeg/qffmpeghwaccel_vaapi.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/multimedia/ffmpeg/qffmpeghwaccel_vaapi.cpp
@@ (anchors; apply with tools/build-patched-qt/apply-0004.py)
-    // ### Check that prime.fourcc is what we expect
-    vaSyncSurface(vaDisplay, vaSurface);
+    // ### Check that prime.fourcc is what we expect
+    if (VAStatus st = vaSyncSurface(vaDisplay, vaSurface); st != VA_STATUS_SUCCESS) {
+        qWarning() << "vaSyncSurface failed:" << st << "- not importing the surface";
+        return nullptr;   // closeObjectsGuard closes the exported fds
+    }
